ooks like a  pretty simple costume but that is not  the case this black jumpsuit is super  restrictive and very hot no not that  kind of hot  we dean that scarlet had to wring out  the sweat from her socks every day she  would get really overheated in her  costume one time she got so hot during  the filming of a fight scene that she  ended up hallucinating  who knew a costume could be so dangerous  she also hated how tight the suit was  Thor was able to have a small fan  installed in his costume but her  costumes were too tight for that she  couldn't wear anything underneath it  whatsoever the conditions of the  jumpsuit caused it to weather easily so  Scarlett went through several of them  during the filming process Ralph Fiennes  as Voldemort Harry Potter fans know that  he-who-must-not-be-named is one of the  creepiest villains of all time this  wizard did so much dark magic that he  basically looked like a snake human  hybrid it wasn't easy to pull off this  look in the movies Ralph's played the  Dark Lord and he has complained about  the makeup process he had to be  completely painted with white makeup to  give him that signature creepy gray look  he had to wear prosthetics to cover up  his eyebrows and give his face the right  shape he also had to wear fake teeth  they got rid of his nose with CGI which  was good for the actor but Ralph got  really tired of the long process wearing  that much makeup and prosthetics can get  really tiring maybe some of his  Voldemort anger came from that Ralph is  a great actor and no one could have  played Voldemort better than him but he  has said that he has considered turning  down future roles if they require a  similar costume that's how bad he hated  it Anne Hathaway as Catwoman everyone  knows Batman's famous frenemy Catwoman  Catwoman was added to the comics to  spice things up  she's been portrayed in films many times  Catwoman is easily recognizable in her  black leather bodysuit and cat mask some  actresses have found the suit really  empowering like Halle Berry but Anne  Hathaway disagreed she hated her costume  with a passion in fact she has called  the suit psychological torture she  became obsessed with how she looked in  it the tight suit really did a number on  her body image she said that even when  she wasn't wearing it she became  obsessed with fitting into it and  looking good  she was so infatuated with working out  to the point that it was unhealthy we  can't imagine having to wear something  that really messes with our self-image  that has to be hard another  catwoman agreed Michelle Pfeiffer who  played Catwoman in the 90s said it was  probably unhealthy she tried to squeeze  into the suit until it hurt  Tom Holland does spider-man Tom Holland  is the latest spider-man a young actor  has stolen fans hearts as the marble  hero spider-man soo is really important  to the story in fact he even tries to  tell Tony Stark in the first movie that  he's nothing without it but the real  suit that he has to wear is not at all  enjoyable first of all the suit is so  tight that he can only wear special  undergarments that aren't exactly  comfortable he also has to remove the  entire thing to answer nature's call  which is no easy task  one version of the suit was just one  piece so the mask was attached this made  it really hard for Tom to stay hydrated  on set the crew had to stick a straw  through the eye socket for him to take  sips of water he also wears a helmet  under the mask  and it can mess with his vision not only  is that uncomfortable but it's also  dangerous his vision was so impeded that  he didn't see a stunt double that was  supposed to fake punch him poor Tom  ended up getting punched in the face for  real as a result are you a total movie  buff you'll fit right in up the things  click that big red subscribe button and  turn on notifications to never miss  another video be sure to check your  notification settings if you're watching  on your phone Anthony Daniels as c-3po  you might not recognize this actor by  name but we bet you recognize his  character the latest Star Wars movie  comes out in December of 2019 and all  generations of fans are excited c-3po is  the super smart droid from the Star Wars  franchise Anthony Daniels has been  playing c-3po since the very first movie  over 40 years ago he has been in almost  every episode of the saga he takes pride  in being the only person who is willing  to wear the suit but he's pretty honest  with how miserable it is to wear it back  in the 1970s the suit injured him almost  as soon as he put it on the first time  the second step he took caused one of  the legs to shattered this drove a sharp  piece of plastic into his foot it was a  big injury that caused him a lot of pain  he also said it's really hot to wear a  lot of the movies have been filmed in  the desert  so that makes it even worse you know  which Hogwarts student in Harry Potter  hated their costume the most keep  watching to find out margot robbie as  Harley Quinn some costumes may not be  physically uncomfortable but they can  really make an actor feel self-conscious  margot robbie plays the criminally  insane partner to the Joker Harley Quinn  Harley is known for wearing sparkly hot  pants and pink and blue pigtails Margot  says the character likes the costume not  because of the suggestive nature but  because it's fun but Margot as the  actress can't stand her costume it was  very revealing and it made her feel very  self-conscious she said she was hyper  aware of her appearance she'd go to eat  hamburgers on her lunch break and worry  about the way she looked in one scene  that was filmed right after lunch she  had to be hosed down it made her white  t-shirt extra clingy and she was not  comfortable at all  Margot wasn't really a fan of the way  her character was portrayed as a flirty  suggestive symbol in the costume  chadwick boseman as Black Panther fans  fell in love with the world of Wakanda  and black panther chadwick boseman is  the perfect actor to play the king and  super hero in the movie two challahs  smart sister designs his black panther  suit is it we're up to Cherie the suit  would be really easy to move and breathe  in but we don't really have wakanda's  technology so Chadwicks costume was not  nearly as cool the costume was so tight  that Chadwick had trouble breathing in  it that's not a good thing considering  all the fight scenes he had to film it  was so tight that it was hard to put on  and even more challenging to move around  in it was also really hot they were  usually filming in 90-degree weather  which made chadwick hate it even more he  sweat a lot and couldn't scratch any  itches chadwick has said that he had to  get into a mental Zen space in order to  get through the scenes Jim Carrey as the  Grinch everyone loves the holiday  classic How the Grinch Stole Christmas  Jim Carrey is just so believable as the  green Christmas hating guy who lives  north of who-ville it might be because  getting into costume was a miserable  process so Jim didn't have to act all  that upset when filming first started it  took eight hours to transform into the  Koran  that's a whole workday and he still had  to film Jim has described the process of  getting the makeup prosthetics and fur  as being buried alive they even had to  bring in a CIA operative who trained Jim  on how to withstand the process that's  super dark for a family holiday movie  eventually they figured out how to get  the process down to a little over two  hours but Jim had to be transformed into  the Grinch over 90 times for filming he  hated it every time we're definitely  going to watch that movie with a new  appreciation Matthew Lewis as Neville  Longbottom Harry Potter fans love  Neville Longbottom he was the shy  awkward kid who ended up leading the  resistance at Hogwarts and slaying the  guinea people have talked for years  about matthew lewis's glow-up after the  movies he no longer looks like the young  Gryffindor we grew up watching on the  big screen but here's the thing he never  really looked like that Matthew had to  wear a fat suit to play Neville for most  of the movies puberty is hard enough but  it was extra hard for him because  everyone thought he was larger than he  actually was even the girls on set  didn't realize it was just a suit it  really did a number on his self-esteem  he also had to wear false teeth that  were yellowish the makeup department put  prosthetics behind his ears to make them  stick out it's hard enough growing up in  Hollywood but having to look extra  awkward is tough knowing this we're not  too surprised that Matthew hated his  Neville costume and that's it for the  ten actors who hated their costumes  which costume from this video do you  think sounds the worst to wear let us  know in the comments section below  thanks for watching don't forget to give  this video a big thumbs up see you next  time  you

